--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: ovg::patch
visibility: public
---
# `ovg::lib` is public and says nothing about mutability, so it is immutable.
# The gate answers `!ref` and nothing else: the tag declares intent to modify
# and is refused, and the two spellings below it declare a priority among
# claimants, which is not a mutation and is not gated (D4.14).
Amend: !node &Amend
  extends: !ref override ../lib/Shared
Take: !node &Take
  <<: override ../lib/Shared
Bare: !node &Bare
  extends: override ../lib/Shared
# `brute` is a prefix on the member and `override` one on the operand, so the
# two compose: the forced write is recorded as W0304 and performed anyway.
Forced: !node &Forced
  brute claim: !ref override ../lib/Shared
  refused: !ref override ../lib/Shared
# `brute` is required for `!ref override` into an immutable scope, so it has to
# reach a clause operand. The operator binds no member, so the `brute` that
# forces it is the one on the member whose value writes the clause (D6.4b).
brute Forceful: !node &Forceful
  extends: !ref override ../lib/Shared
# Visibility is decided in pass 4, in front of the lookup, and neither word
# changes that: a target out of view resolved to nothing.
Blind: !node &Blind
  peek: !ref override ../vault/Secret
